--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DeepSeek-V4-Flash -- deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

MIT License. The GGUF files state it themselves in `general.license`.

The model is NOT redistributed by this project. The README points at the source
and the user fetches it. The quantisation actually used is
`unsloth/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF` (`UD-IQ3_XXS`, 95.9 GiB, four files), which is
unsloth's own artefact and carries whatever terms that repository states.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The CUDA backend is built against NVIDIA's CUDA Toolkit -- version 13.3 on the
development machine -- and is subject to the NVIDIA Software License Agreement
and the CUDA Supplement to it.

This repository ships no CUDA runtime libraries: the build tree's `bin/Release`
holds eleven files, all of them `ggml-*`, `llama-*` or `mtmd`, and neither
`cudart` nor `cuBLAS` is among them. Wherever a release does ship NVIDIA
redistributable libraries alongside the binaries, those files stay under
NVIDIA's own terms and are NOT covered by the MIT grant above. NVIDIA permits
redistribution of the libraries it designates as redistributable, under the
conditions stated in that agreement.

Whether the binaries require such a library to be present at all is UNMEASURED.
`dumpbin /dependents` on `ggml-cuda.dll` settles it, and it is point 1 of
issue #57.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Google Sans Code -- cli/fonts/
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 -- not MIT.

Two `.ttf` files ship in `cli/fonts/`. The full licence text sits beside them in
`cli/fonts/OFL.txt` and must stay there: under the OFL a font may be bundled and
redistributed ONLY with that notice. `cli/test_crow.py` asserts the file is
present, because without it redistribution is a licence violation that nothing
else in the build would catch.
